<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>

	<!--
		Big and Small - Heaven and Hell joined up with Nephilim Xenotype Reborn.
		  - The Heaven faction can roll nephilim, and its melee servitors always do.
		  - With EBSG Framework and Ideology, the Heaven faction requires the gracetouched meme.
		  - The four angel and demon xenotypes gain the grace, resurrection, heal and holy hymn genes.
		  - The grigori description is rewritten and Big and Small's own nephilim is renamed to goliath, so the two
		    mods do not both offer something called a nephilim.
		This folder only loads when Heaven and Hell is active (see loadFolders.xml); the partner mods are gated inside.
		The mod gates sit on <li> nodes inside sequences, not on the <Operation> itself: RimWorld reads
		MayRequire only on list elements, so an <Operation MayRequire="..."> node loads and applies
		unconditionally.
		Name fix applied on review: the original checked for a mod named "Nephilim Xenotype". Mod-name checks
		are exact matches and the mod is named "Nephilim Xenotype Reborn", so those checks never fired. The
		packageId sov.nephilim is used here instead, which cannot drift the same way.
		The original sat behind a Too Many Mods setting toggle (TMM_BS_NephilimBeliarIntegration, default on).
		That toggle is dropped: the folder gate and the MayRequire checks already keep it inert unless the
		mods it joins are installed.

		Verified against the current 1.6 releases: every gene, meme and xenotype referenced exists, the Heaven faction
		has both a xenotypeChances block and a requiredMemes list, the melee servitor has a xenotypeChances block, and
		none of the four xenotypes already carries any of the genes being added. All eight operations land.
		Split by category into the MMMM Integrations sub-mods: this copy holds only the Factions ops (factions, pawn kinds, traders and royal titles).
	-->
	<Operation Class="PatchOperationSequence">
		<operations>
			<li Class="PatchOperationSequence" MayRequire="sov.nephilim">
				<operations>
					<li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
						<xpath>
							Defs/FactionDef[defName="BS_Heaven"]/xenotypeSet/xenotypeChances</xpath>
						<value>
							<GS_Nephilim>0.1</GS_Nephilim>
						</value>
					</li>
					<li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
						<xpath>
							Defs/PawnKindDef[defName="BS_ServitorMelee"]/xenotypeSet/xenotypeChances</xpath>
						<value>
							<GS_Nephilim>99999</GS_Nephilim>
						</value>
					</li>
				</operations>
			</li>

			<li Class="PatchOperationSequence" MayRequire="sov.nephilim,ebsg.framework,Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">
				<operations>
					<li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
						<xpath>Defs/FactionDef[defName="BS_Heaven"]/requiredMemes</xpath>
						<value>
							<li>GS_Gracetouched</li>
						</value>
					</li>
				</operations>
			</li>
		</operations>
	</Operation>

</Patch>
